      "name": "Kramer vs. Kramer",
      "type": "urn:entity",
      "properties": {
        "release_year": 1979,
        "content_rating": "PG",
        "plot_themes_description": "The film examines the emotional and legal fallout of divorce, the challenges of single parenthood, shifting gender roles, and the tension between career ambition and familial responsibility.",
        "description": "Kramer vs. Kramer (1979), written and directed by Robert Benton and starring Dustin Hoffman, Meryl Streep and Justin Henry, is a drama about a Manhattan advertising executive who must suddenly parent his young son after his wife leaves. Over months of small domestic scenes the film traces the father's emotional growth and the bond he forms with his child, then escalates into a wrenching custody battle when the mother returns. Thematically it interrogates divorce, shifting gender roles, and the costs of career ambition on family life, presented with understated visuals and powerful, authentic performances."
      },
