        "plot_themes_description": "The story examines resilience and leadership through personal disability, family tension, painful rehabilitation, and the determination to preserve political purpose.",
        "description": "Sunrise at Campobello (1960), directed by Vincent J. Donehue and adapted from Dore Schary's play, stars Ralph Bellamy, Greer Garson, and Hume Cronyn in a biographical drama about Franklin D. Roosevelt's struggle with polio. The film dramatizes his painful rehabilitation, fraught family relationships, and the political maneuvering that surrounds his attempt to remain publicly relevant. Focused on intimate performances and moral resolve, the picture explores themes of perseverance, leadership, and resilience with an earnest, dignified tone."
